1
00:00:00,400 --> 00:00:07,544
Suppose I'm Rohin, an AP accountant. Every week I check invoices from our staffing agency, Halcyon, by hand.

2
00:00:07,800 --> 00:00:13,703
Ramp Teach lets Rohin show that check once, so every bill after already arrives checked, with the proof.

3
00:00:13,803 --> 00:00:18,919
So let's say it's close week, so I'm recording myself reviewing this month's Halcyon invoice.

4
00:00:19,019 --> 00:00:22,259
Every rate on it has to match the rate card in our contract,

5
00:00:22,359 --> 00:00:24,842
and nobody should be billed twice for the same week.

6
00:00:24,942 --> 00:00:28,776
Then I check each person's hours against their approved timecard.

7
00:00:28,876 --> 00:00:32,842
Maya's approved for 40 hours, so billed hours can't go over that.

8
00:00:32,942 --> 00:00:35,640
Sam's approved for 36.

9
00:00:35,740 --> 00:00:39,908
If anything's off, I dispute it and ask the agency for a credit memo.

10
00:00:40,111 --> 00:00:44,392
When I stop, each thing I said shows up, linked to the step it was about.

11
00:00:44,492 --> 00:00:52,050
Rohin, while you worked, the recorder saved each click with the exact element you hit, and every sentence you said with its timing, matched to the clicks around it.

12
00:00:52,150 --> 00:00:55,875
Your click shows where the evidence is, and your sentences say the rules.

13
00:00:56,292 --> 00:00:58,454
So now I'm going to send it to Ramp.

14
00:01:00,225 --> 00:01:07,979
Rohin's recording becomes a workflow, and when the next invoice comes in, an agent runs that workflow in its own browser, bringing back the same evidence.

15
00:01:08,279 --> 00:01:11,678
Bill Pay is learning my review, one stage at a time.

16
00:01:11,778 --> 00:01:13,337
Here's what it learned.

17
00:01:13,537 --> 00:01:16,685
Each rule points back to what I said and where I clicked,

18
00:01:16,785 --> 00:01:20,189
and my recording keeps my words lined up with my clicks.

19
00:01:23,735 --> 00:01:30,017
Claude reads your recording and writes the workflow: each rule with the words and click that it came from, and where the proof lives.

20
00:01:30,117 --> 00:01:35,517
It learns what to check and where to find it, writing real deterministic math code to spot differences.

21
00:01:35,691 --> 00:01:40,023
Here it passed its evals, so this is now our active workflow.

22
00:01:40,123 --> 00:01:43,595
Just now, a new invoice from Halcyon hit my approval queue,

23
00:01:43,695 --> 00:01:47,166
so we can see Ramp picks the right workflow and starts its agent.

24
00:01:48,799 --> 00:01:52,944
While it does that, I can watch the agent's own browser right here in the bill,

25
00:01:53,044 --> 00:01:56,191
and it also pulls each timecard the same way I did.

26
00:01:56,291 --> 00:02:00,627
The run lives under Workflows, with every model turn and tool call,

27
00:02:00,727 --> 00:02:04,665
and each step shows its tokens, cost and request ID.

28
00:02:04,765 --> 00:02:08,983
So every fact gets reread from its page by plain code.

29
00:02:09,083 --> 00:02:14,242
It found three problems and $3,500 to credit back,

30
00:02:14,342 --> 00:02:19,648
and this is where I can dispute it, as the agent never approves or pays anything itself.

31
00:02:19,748 --> 00:02:25,925
The agent gets its own browser, and each turn Claude sees the page as an outline, picks the action, and gets the result.

32
00:02:26,025 --> 00:02:30,532
It only records the facts with the page that they came from, and code turns them into pass or fail.

33
00:02:30,632 --> 00:02:33,355
Claude writes the receipt, and then you make the call.

34
00:02:36,845 --> 00:02:40,251
Next, this is a clean invoice from the same agency,

35
00:02:41,219 --> 00:02:45,752
and since everything checks out, just one click from me moves it on to payment.

36
00:02:48,965 --> 00:02:55,586
We test the checks against past corrections, the learnings against recordings with known answers, and the whole review end to end.

37
00:02:55,686 --> 00:03:01,444
Every Claude call is logged with its tokens, its cost, and request ID that we can look up for observability.

38
00:03:01,644 --> 00:03:07,458
Today, this one recording from Rohin can become a tested workflow, with evidence behind every single recommendation.

39
00:03:07,558 --> 00:03:13,325
In the future, we see integrations with Teams and Slack to attach evidence from there to receipts as well.

40
00:03:13,625 --> 00:03:15,058
Thank you.
